        "type": "User",
        "site_admin": false,
        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "Just a note to other reviewers: it looks fine to just drop `FD_SET(s, &err);` instead of moving it to under `if (events.requested & RecvEvent)`. We do not expect and do not care about any \"exceptional conditions\":\n\nfrom `select(2)`:\n>     exceptfds\n>            The  file  descriptors  in this set are watched for \"exceptional conditions\".  For examples of some excep‐\n>            tional conditions, see the discussion of POLLPRI in poll(2).\n\nfrom `poll(2)`:\n>      POLLPRI\n>            There is some exceptional condition on the file descriptor.  Possibilities include:\n>            •  There is out-of-band data on a TCP socket (see tcp(7)).\n>            •  A pseudoterminal master in packet mode has seen a state change on the slave (see ioctl_tty(2)).\n>            •  A cgroup.events file has been modified (see cgroups(7)).\n\nAlso, our `poll()` branch does not do `POLLPRI`.\n\nHowever! https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winsock2/nf-winsock2-select:\n\n> exceptfds:\n>    If processing a connect call (nonblocking), connection attempt failed.\n>    OOB data is available for reading (only if SO_OOBINLINE is disabled).\n\nSo, `FD_SET(s, &err);` is needed on Windows to handle our non-blocking `connect()`s.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-26T14:50:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T15:08:31Z",
